00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a fascinating
documentary

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was about something
that happened,

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was this
Hulk Hogan Gawker trial...

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...which basically
bankrupted Gawker,

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then the issues in it
have sort of become

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.580
a little bit more important now
maybe even than they were then.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.415
But tell us a little bit
about what got you started

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
on this story.
-Yeah, I mean, I was

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
really, really interested
in this case,

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:22.055
this sort of trial between
Hulk Hogan and Gawker Media.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.723 size:81% position:41%
I just thought it was
interesting by itself.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.926
You know, this was the first
time a sex-tape case like this

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:27.761 size:84% position:42% line:92%
had ever gone to trial.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:30.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So they had -- They basically
put the sex tape online.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:35.435
-Yeah, so, Hulk Hogan was filmed
having sex with the wife --

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.271 size:84% position:42%
-The key to a sex tape.
-The key to a sex tape.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With the wife
of his then-best friend,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bubba the Love Sponge...
-Right.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.780 size:88% position:44%
-...who is a shock-jock
radio deejay in Florida.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.848 line:92%
So, this tape gets out there.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people
speculate about it.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's some stills
posted I think on --

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:56.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe on TMZ and some other --
The Dirty or something.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.657 line:92%
And then eventually Gawker posts

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:01.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
an edited-down version of
this tape, along with a post.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that starts
this really lengthy

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of trial,
this battle between them.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:09.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And during the trial,
Hulk Hogan made a distinction

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
between the character
of Hulk Hogan

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.474 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and his actual --

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
the actual guy, Terry Bollea.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And because part
of what Gawker argued

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that they published
this sex tape

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.782
because it refuted things
that Hulk Hogan had said

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
about his own sexual prowess.
Is that correct?

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:28.755
-Yes, and this was a defense
that the Hogan team brought.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.823 line:92%
It was new to this trial.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.091 line:92%
They hadn't even mentioned this

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the previous
incarnations of this,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they made a distinction
between Hulk Hogan

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the private person,
Terry Bollea.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.833 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And it was fascinating.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, basically
their argument --

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, "Look, you've
talked about this sex tape --

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:46.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
this sex incident many times
on Howard Stern's show,

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
in fact,
in very graphic details.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.311 line:92%
So why is this so private?

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you've actually
brought this into the public.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've made it newsworthy
yourself."

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said,
"Well, that's different.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:01.020
That was me as Hulk Hogan
bragging about my sex life,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's different
than me as Terry Bollea."

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they actually
asked about his --

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you can
say this -- 10-inch penis.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Once you say "10-inch,"
they're gonna finish it.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so that actually
becomes a thing.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Hulk Hogan on the trial,
or Mr. Bollea, says,

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:21.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Actually I don't have
a 10-inch penis.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hulk Hogan does.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.179 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But me, not so much."

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.247 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-This is a crazy --

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
This sounds like
just the craziest trial.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Hulk Hogan wins
this $50-million settlement.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it 50?
-It's $140 million.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.089 line:92%
-$140 million. My goodness.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, I mean,
that was the initial verdict.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.192 line:92%
-And so that bankrupts Gawker.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.995
Now, one of the things
that's interesting is, you know,

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are a lot of people
that would say

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gawker made some
editorial choices

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:50.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were sort of beyond
what is considered

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.105 size:88% position:44% line:92%
journalism with dignity.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.607 line:92%
But ultimately the question is,

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you also have to
protect the free speech

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.178 line:92%
or the rights to the free press

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.446
when they're doing things
that you don't agree with?

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that the fear of press
going forward,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.685 size:88% position:44%
is that Gawker basically
was put out of business

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.419 size:75% position:38% line:92%
by this one decision

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.122
and that other people will use
this same technique to take down

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:12.225
any website or any news sources
that they don't like?

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I mean,
you're completely right.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.829
It's a complex story, and I
think that's one of the reasons

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
why I personally found it
so compelling.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.300 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It's not an easy story.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I kind of
found it interesting

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it's difficult
in some ways

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:28.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it is on the edges
of acceptability with speech.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a little like

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The People vs. Larry Flynt"
kind of territory.

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:35.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that dramatic verdict
that actually silences Gawker

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:36.916 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and then the revelation

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Silicon Valley investor
Peter Thiel

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.420 size:88% position:44% line:92%
was actually bankrolling

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
